WEBVTT

00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:16,360
A cause is a benign tumors, similar to the causes of cancerous tumors, toxic, overload, etc.

00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:22,360
If you have a benign tumor, does that tell us something about our health that needs to change?

00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:29,360
Well, yeah, whenever you have anything wrong like a benign tumor or a cancerous tumor,

00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:37,360
or, you know, any type of side or symptom is a side or symptom that something may need to change.

00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:43,360
I say it may need to change because it could have been something that you were exposed to years ago

00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:47,360
that you don't have that exposure, you already changed that.

00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:52,360
For instance, maybe you were living in a moldy house when you were a kid.

00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:59,360
You picked up a lot of micotoxin, and that has caused damage and maybe even caused a tumor.

00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:02,360
But if you did a micotoxin test today, your body had cleared it out.

00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:09,360
That was maybe 20 years ago when you inadvertently cleared it out because your body is constantly trying to detoxify.

00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,360
But it did lead lasting damage.

00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:16,360
So it might not be something that you need the current change to.

00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:20,360
But maybe you need the current change to help decrease the growth of that tumor.

00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:27,360
So there's a lot of cancerous tumors like Lypomas.

00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:38,360
Lypomas can have congenital ties to them, too, in their genetic predisposition to Lypomas.

00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:45,360
A lot of non-cancerous tumors are very idiopathic, but they don't know what causes them.

00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:49,360
The hypothesis is that it's the same as cancer.

00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:55,360
It can be toxin, et cetera, that can lead to that, but there can be genetic pieces to that, too.

00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:59,360
But yeah, like anything, you do want to investigate current exposure to different things.

00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,360
You do want to investigate toxic levels.

00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:08,360
And you do want to support detoxification pathways, et cetera, especially depending on where the benign tumor is.

00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:13,360
If you have a benign tumor in your head, that's a space occupied lesion where you have only so much space.

00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:18,360
So that can cause just as much problem as a malignant tumor in the brain, too.

